// @expect-error A 'char' is a code point rather than a quantity, so it has no 'double' form of its own. Write 'as double' where the code point's number is what you mean.
// A code point is a name for a character, not a measurement, so letting it drift into a
// floating-point number would turn a mistake into 65.0 rather than reporting it.
main() -> int {
    double code = 'A';
    return code > 0.0 ? 0 : 1;
}
